<BaseLayout title="About Casey Manos">
	<h1>About Casey Manos</h1>
	<p>
		This is Casey Manos's personal website: a place for a biography, public projects, a resume, and
		writing about engineering and running. Casey is a founding engineer at Adapt and previously
		worked as a backend engineer at JPMC. He received a B.S. in Computer Engineering from Ohio State
		University. His interests include track and field, competitive running, and the science of
		training. The writing section contains personal accounts of building and debugging software.
		Those accounts describe particular projects and moments in time; they are not official
		documentation for the companies or tools mentioned. For professional background, see the resume.
		For questions or corrections, use the contact page.
	</p>
